---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About ${siteConfig.brandName}`}
  description="How LearnChineseNews started, and why we are building better reading tools for intermediate Chinese learners."
>
  <section class="container about-wrap">
    <h1>About {siteConfig.brandName}</h1>
    <article class="card">
      <p>
        Hi, thanks for your interest in our little project. I started learning Chinese in 2021 and picking up the
        first couple hundred vocab words was easy. I found a frequency list and learned the first few hundred words.
        I am a heritage Chinese learner, so I always had some exposure to spoken Chinese, but I was never able to
        read Chinese because literacy takes active study.
      </p>
      <p>
        I decided to learn to read Chinese at a native level within five years, but after the basics there is a real
        gap between native books and articles and what intermediate learners (HSK4 and HSK5) can read without looking
        up every other sentence. So I decided to build LearnChineseNews around Chinese New Year 2026 to bridge that
        gap. I built a simple version with pinyin and segmentation, then added a basic CEDICT and Pleco integration.
      </p>
      <p>
        What I realized is that a few practical tools can make even complex native-level articles approachable.
        Eventually I added sentence-level translations, AI-assisted study tools, and more media sources so I could
        always find content I already wanted to read.
      </p>
      <p>
        Now we are getting ready for internal beta testing with a few dozen users. If you are an intermediate Chinese
        learner and want to try new tools for learning by reading real native content, I would love your feedback so
        we can decide our next development path.
      </p>
      <p class="contact-line">
        Reach me at
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-wrap {
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3.2vw, 2.3rem);
  }

  article p {
    margin: 0 0 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .contact-line {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .contact-line a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
